  data:  # c866
    kind: meta_invariant  # c866
    title: "Assessment pipeline continuity: prior context injection and aggregation resilience"  # c866
    status: needs_human_review  # c866
    priority: 2  # c866
    parent:  # c866
    tags:  # c866
    - bakeoff  # c866
    - process-health  # c866
    before: []  # c866
    duplicate_of: []  # c866
    not_duplicate_of: []  # c866
    pr_ref:  # c866
    justification:  # c866
    description: "SOURCE: Process health synthesis §3.1, §3.3, §3.6, recommendations 7 and 11.\n\nPROBLEM (two related gaps):\n\n1. PRIOR CONTEXT NOT INJECTED: The DEEP reflect pipeline uses fixed structured tasks (A/B/C) with no mechanism to include prior assessment findings. Each LLM assessor sees the current output fresh — it cannot distinguish \"new issue\" from \"previously identified and addressed issue.\" This causes the same themes to be re-raised across cohorts even when specific instances were already fixed. The BROAD pipeline has stratified question pools including journal questions, but BROAD has not been used during this bakeoff and may never have been exercised.\n\n2. AGGREGATION FRAGILE TO SESSION DEATH: 5 cohort/iteration combos (004/iter-002, 006/iter-002, 011/iter-003, 011/iter-006, 012/iter-001) had assessment YAMLs written by subagents but no summary.yaml generated, because the spawning session ran out of context before subagents completed. The aggregation step silently dropped out of the pipeline. Subsequent autonomous sessions operated with incomplete information about what the bakeoff found.\n\nROOT CAUSE: Any step that depends on all subagents completing cannot live in the session that spawned them.\n\nOPTIONS FOR PRIOR CONTEXT:\n(a) Inject improvement_ideas and overall_verdict from the previous cohort's assessment of the same repo into the DEEP prompt.\n(b) Add a lightweight \"prior findings\" section to the fixed DEEP prompt template.\n(c) Have the assessor read summary.yaml from the previous iteration as part of the prompt context.\n\nOPTIONS FOR AGGREGATION RESILIENCE:\n(a) Have each assessment subagent check if it's the last repo and trigger aggregation.\n(b) Add a bakeoff-features post-assess step that the next autonomous session runs before starting new work.\n(c) Make aggregation a hook that runs on session startup, checking for unaggregated cohorts.\n(d) Decouple aggregation from the spawning session entirely (cron or pre-work checklist item)."  # c866
    fields:  # c866
      statement: "The bakeoff assessment pipeline must inject prior findings into new assessments and must not silently drop the aggregation step when the spawning session dies before subagents complete."  # c866
